.TH RBAC\-AUDIT 1 "2026-09" "rbac-auditor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rbac-audit \- readable RBAC reports from a live Kubernetes cluster
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rbac-audit
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports who can do what in a cluster, and which of those grants look wrong:
wildcard grants, cluster-admin bindings, ServiceAccounts no pod references,
and bindings that point at subjects which do not exist.
.PP
With no command it produces a report.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B report
Full Markdown report: findings, then inventory. Accepts
.BI \-\-ignore\-file " PATH"
(suppressions, default
.IR .rbac-audit-ignore ),
.BI \-\-html " PATH"
to also write a self-contained HTML report, and
.BI \-\-s3 " s3://BUCKET/PREFIX"
to upload it (with
.BR \-\-sse ,
default AES256).
.TP
.B dump
Raw JSON snapshot, for diffing or archiving.
.TP
.BI diff " OLD.json"
Compare a previous
.B dump
against the live cluster.
.TP
.BI who-can " VERB RESOURCE"
Subjects allowed VERB on RESOURCE, e.g.
.BR "who-can delete pods" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on\-findings
Exit non-zero when the report contains findings. The CI gate.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .rbac-audit-ignore
Suppressions, so that an accepted grant stops being reported.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed and, where gated, found nothing.
.TP
.B non-zero
Findings with
.BR \-\-fail\-on\-findings ,
or a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Report on the current context:
.PP
.RS
.B rbac-audit report
.RE
.PP
Gate CI:
.PP
.RS
.B rbac-audit report \-\-fail\-on\-findings
.RE
.PP
Who can delete pods:
.PP
.RS
.B rbac-audit who-can delete pods
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kubectl (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/rbac-auditor
.UE
